  "damping_selector": "previous evaluator iff exact represented gamma <=411/4096; new shifted evaluator otherwise. Frequency selectors remain omega<=577/128. Inputs passed unchanged.",
  "residual_theorem": "For each exact meanfree frozen state vc, ||rz|| <=sqrt(d2)+sqrt(nu2)+|z-zc|*||vc||L2/2; |Hz-Jz(vc)|<=kappa||rz||^2, kappa=sqrt(1+(omega/(2gamma))^2). Jz=Jc-(z-zc) integral vc^2. No exact Galerkin premise.",
  "rectangle_proof": "Positive omega,gamma ranges imply monotone omega^2 and gamma*omega. Bound each absolute parameter component by the maximum of the two endpoint magnitudes; sum squares bounds |z-zc|^2 even if component maxima occur at different corners. Kappa uses omega upper and gamma lower. New center gamma is interior, not a lower endpoint.",
  "parameter_semantics": "Input parameters denote exact represented binary64 values. Exact rational damping centers1/10 and101/1000 are not their nearest float words; center-constant quantization is included. No input parsing, measurement or Hertz calibration claim.",
